%S A401015 0,1,4,2,6,9,4,2,5,6,7,1,8,3,6,1,8,2,3,4,7,5,9,3,7,5,8,9,1,4,2,6,9,4,
%T A401015 2,5,6,7,1,8,3,6,1,8,2,3,4,7,5,9,3,7,5,8,9,1,4,2,6,9,4,2,5,6,7,1,8,3,
%U A401015 6,1,8,2,3,4,7,5,9,3,7,5,8,9,1,4,2,6,9,4,2,5,6,7
%N A401015 Digital roots of A006527(n), the number of unit tetrahedra in a regular tetrahedron subdivided into a tetrahedral-octahedral lattice.
%C A401015 For n > 0, the sequence is periodic with least period 27.
%C A401015 Each integer from 1 through 9 occurs exactly three times in each period. Consequently, the sum of the terms in one period is 135 and their arithmetic mean is 5.
%C A401015 This sequence belongs to a family of 27-term digital-root cycles associated with three-dimensional figurate numbers, including the tetrahedral numbers A000292 (as noted by Ant King, Oct 18 2012), square pyramidal numbers A000330, and octahedral numbers A005900. Each of these cycles contains every integer from 1 through 9 exactly three times, with a period sum of 135.
%C A401015 In particular, the underlying tetrahedral-cell counts A006527(n), together with the octahedral-cell counts A000292(n-1), sum to A006003(n) = (n^3 + n)/2. The digital roots of this sum coincide with A267017, the digital roots of the stella octangula numbers A007588, since A007588(n) - A006003(n) = 9*A000292(n-1). Combining the underlying counts of two geometrically related sequences with 27-period digital roots yields the 9-period sequence A267017.
%F A401015 a(n) = A010888(A006527(n)) = digital_root((n^3 + 2*n)/3).
%F A401015 For n >= 1, a(n) = 1 + (((n^3 + 2*n)/3 - 1) mod 9), with a(0) = 0.
%F A401015 For n >= 2, a(n) = digital_root(A000292(n) + A000292(n-2)).
%F A401015 a(n+27) = a(n) for n >= 1.
%e A401015 For n = 3, A006527(3) = 11, so a(3) = digital_root(11) = 1 + 1 = 2.
%e A401015 For n = 5, A006527(5) = 45, so a(5) = digital_root(45) = 4 + 5 = 9.
%e A401015 For n = 28, A006527(28) = 7336, so a(28) = digital_root(7 + 3 + 3 + 6) = digital_root(19) = 1, beginning the next 27-term cycle.
%Y A401015 Cf. A006527 (underlying unit-tetrahedron counts), A010888 (digital roots), A000292 (tetrahedral numbers), A000330 (square pyramidal numbers), A005900 (octahedral numbers).
%K A401015 nonn,easy,base,new
